 "subsets": "Aregger 2020 query screens (FASN, ACACA, C12orf49, SREBF1/2, LDLR, PDK1, SLC16A3) are present in this dataset re-scored with qGI, but all in the 'min' medium arm, so they are not in the SLB rich-medium measurements. Xiao 2024: not identified in the Data S1 metadata (no publication column); not verified.",
 "verdict": "include",
 "verdict_reason": "Own replication passes clearly: SLB rule applied to one independent screen of the same query, scored by another, AUROC 0.87 pooled (15,337 positives across 28 replicated queries, all 20 ordered screen pairs 0.79-0.95); per-query mean 0.79 vs 0.49 when scored by an unrelated query's screen, so replication is query-specific, not library-gene fitness. Hit rate 0.37% is plausible. There is no same-line cross-study overlap (7 pairs with CHyMErA HAP1), so there can be no contradiction. Cross-line overlap is weak (pooled 0.54 for 166 positives), as expected for non-paralog GIs across lines. Fitness alone gives 0.61-0.69 (<0.8). Caveat: only 28/127 queries have replicate screens; labels are hub-structured (127 queries x ~17.7k genes)."
}